codex-acp 1.1.4 served-identity passthrough

Upstreamable changes:

1. In CodexACPAgent.newSession, pass
   developerInstructions: request._meta?.developerInstructions
   to codexClient.threadStart.
2. In CodexACPAgent.loadSession, pass the same field to
   codexClient.threadResume.
3. In CodexEventHandler.createUpdateEvent, translate account/updated into:
   {
     sessionUpdate: "session_info_update",
     _meta: { codex: { accountUpdated: notification.params } }
   }

The executable, idempotent form lives in Tightbeam.Harness.Codex because
codex-acp is installed per host at runtime rather than committed in this
repository.

Astra API-key discovery hotfix:

4. In CodexAcpClient.fetchAvailableModels, request model/list with
   includeHidden: true, then retain only !model.hidden or id === "gpt-6-astra".
   Preserve pagination and the engine's exact metadata. Codex 0.153.2 marks
   Astra hidden in API-key mode; do not expose other hidden entries or synthesize
   missing models. See docs/astra-api-hotfix.md for recorded evidence and the
   remaining release gates.
